Runtime content packages (games/platinum/pc/src/pc_modfs.c, compiled for
D; pc/mods/README.md): a package's narc/<nitro path>/<index> file replaces
that NARC member. Every member read of D goes through this file's readers
(the by-id-pair helpers and the NARC_* object API, which msgdata.c, the
graphics loaders and the recompiled asm call by name), so they ask the
claim table first, as Platinum's src/narc.c patch does: a claimed member
is read from the package with its own length (sizes, allocations and
NARC_GetMemberSize see the new length), NARC_New grows num_files by
planted appends, and NARC_ReadFile continues a claimed member
sequentially. Unclaimed reads are the ROM's, byte for byte. NARC_FindID
maps a path to its NarcId for the PC_MODFS_PROBE_NARC probe
(pc/game/pc_dp_modfs.c).

